second artist, birth date for a different person, or second sport is evidence to retain it. Check each proposed deletion once more against all originals before producing the final short list.\nInput: {\"question\": \"What is another common name for the Hummingbird Bush?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 204, \"text\": \"Anisacanthus quadrifidus Anisacanthus quadrifidus is a species of flowering plant native to west and south-central Texas in the United States and adjacent northern Mexico down through the state of Oaxaca.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d00\", \"start\": 205, \"end\": 327, \"text\": \"It is an increasingly common ornamental shrub in Texas and is cultivated in other parts of the Southwestern United States.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d00\", \"start\": 328, \"end\": 531, \"text\": \"It is known by a variety of names including flame acanthus, Wright's desert honeysuckle, hummingbird bush, Wright acanthus, Wright anisacanth, Texas firecracker, Mexican flame and Wright's Mexican flame.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d00\", \"start\": 532, \"end\": 643, \"text\": \"\\\"Wright\\\" refers to American botanist Charles Wright who collected samples of the plant in the mid-19th century.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d00\", \"start\": 644, \"end\": 670, \"text\": \"Some sources also refer to\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 149, \"text\": \"Justicia californica Justicia californica is a species of flowering shrub native to the deserts of southern California, Arizona, and northern Mexico.\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01\", \"start\": 150, \"end\": 283, \"text\": \"Its common names include chuparosa (or chiparosa, both colloquial Spanish terms for \\\"hummingbird\\\"), hummingbird bush, and beloperone.\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01\", \"start\": 284, \"end\": 374, \"text\": \"It is one of the northernmost distributed species of the mostly tropical genus \\\"Justicia\\\".\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01\", \"start\": 375, \"end\": 475, \"text\": \"This is a low bush which grows in dry, hot regions in the sand or rocky terrain of the desert floor.\"}, \"D2S5\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01\", \"start\": 476, \"end\": 519, \"text\": \"For a short time it bears succulent leaves.\"}, \"D2S6\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01\", \"start\": 520, \"end\": 628, \"text\": \"It loses its leaves and then produces plentiful tubular flowers, usually in shades of bright to deep red, or\"}, \"D3S1\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 152, \"text\": \"Grevillea thelemanniana Grevillea thelemanniana, the spider-net grevillea or hummingbird bush, is a small, spreading shrub endemic to Western Australia.\"}, \"D3S2\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02\", \"start\": 153, \"end\": 279, \"text\": \"The species occurs in the Perth region in low-lying areas on sandy and sandy-clay soils which are generally wet in the winter.\"}, \"D3S3\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02\", \"start\": 280, \"end\": 371, \"text\": \"\\\"Grevillea thelemanniana\\\" is a small, spreading shrub, that grows to between high and wide.\"}, \"D3S4\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02\", \"start\": 372, \"end\": 437, \"text\": \"Dark green leaves are divided into narrow segments, and are long.\"}, \"D3S5\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02\", \"start\": 438, \"end\": 599, \"text\": \"The clusters of pink or bright red and yellow tipped flowers appear between late autumn and late spring, and can also appear in any season in garden cultivation.\"}, \"D3S6\": {\"document_number\": 3, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02\", \"start\": 600, \"end\": 632, \"text\": \"A number of former subspecies of\"}, \"D4S1\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d03\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 106, \"text\": \"food sources ( such as a feeder ) against other hummingbirds , attempting to ensure a future food supply .\"}, \"D4S2\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d03\", \"start\": 107, \"end\": 278, \"text\": \"[ 2 ] Additionally , hummingbirds have an enlarged hippocampus , a brain region facilitating spatial memory used to map flowers previously visited during nectar foraging .\"}, \"D4S3\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d03\", \"start\": 279, \"end\": 339, \"text\": \"[ 193 ] Beak specializations [ edit ] Curved beak ( approx .\"}, \"D4S4\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d03\", \"start\": 340, \"end\": 524, \"text\": \"90 o ) of the white-tipped sicklebill Centropogon flowers Coevolution of the sicklebill beak curve facilitates both nectar feeding and pollination of long tubular Centropogon flowers .\"}, \"D4S5\": {\"document_number\": 4, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d03\", \"start\": 525, \"end\": 586, \"text\": \"[ 194 ] The shapes of hummingbird beaks ( also called bills )\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"Hummingbird Bush\", \"scope\": \"common name\", \"claim\": \"Flame acanthus is another common name for the Hummingbird Bush.\", \"answer\": \"Flame acanthus\", \"quote\": \"It is known by a variety of names including flame acanthus, Wright's desert honeysuckle, hummingbird bush, Wright acanthus, Wright anisacanth, Texas firecracker, Mexican flame and Wright's Mexican flame.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"Hummingbird Bush\", \"scope\": \"common name\", \"claim\": \"Another common name for the Hummingbird Bush is chuparosa.\", \"answer\": \"chuparosa\", \"quote\": \"Its common names include chuparosa (or chiparosa, both colloquial Spanish terms for \\\"hummingbird\\\"), hummingbird bush, and beloperone.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0311-9411879e193a:d02:c0\", \"entity\": \"Hummingbird Bush\", \"scope\": \"common name\", \"claim\": \"Another common name for the Hummingbird Bush is spider-net grevillea.\", \"answer\": \"spider-net grevillea\", \"quote\": \"Grevillea thelemanniana Grevillea thelemanniana, the spider-net grevillea or hummingbird bush, is a small, spreading shrub endemic to Western Australia.\", \"original_document_number\": 3}], \"R5_answers\": [\"flame acanthus\", \"chuparosa\", \"spider-net grevillea\", \"Wright's desert honeysuckle\", \"Wright acanthus\", \"Wright anisacanth\", \"Texas firecracker\", \"Mexican flame\", \"Wright's Mexican flame\", \"beloperone\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"flame acanthus\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C1\", \"answer\": \"chuparosa\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C2\", \"answer\": \"spider-net grevillea\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C3\", \"answer\": \"Wright's desert honeysuckle\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C4\", \"answer\": \"Wright acanthus\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C5\", \"answer\": \"Wright anisacanth\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C6\", \"answer\": \"Texas firecracker\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}, {\"id\": \"C7\", \"answer\": \"Mexican flame\", \"origin\": 